<!--Post: 13106--><!--Time: 1114184514-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13106"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Beck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Beck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 22, 2005 - 8:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->OK, so it&#39;s a poor source of information, but the Enquirer is reporting that Raider has colon cancer. I doubt it&#39;s true, but then again, wasn&#39;t that a popular theory on this board on why he started communicating again? Anyways, this is what KAKE had to say about it. Cancer or not, this trial needs to happen now, enough time has passed for these victims. The family and friends shouldn&#39;t need to wait any longer for this.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1496137.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1496137.html</a> <BR>My initial reaction? &#34;Oh WTF now?&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13106-->
<!--Post: 13107--><!--Time: 1114185621-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13107"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 22, 2005 - 9:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Beck, I feel just like you.  This s.o.b. is STILL managing to have complete control even behind bars.  Allthough, it was speculated before, a disease could have been what brought him out of hiding.....but I don&#39;t know legal aspects of what happens if a defendant is ill..gravely ill..I certainly will not be capable of any pity if he does has cancer...I hope his a&#42;&#42; turns inside out and falls out...<IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0> <BR>I could care less other than justice being served. <BR>There is another thread with a poster &#34;Phoenix&#34; I do believe he is an attorney...I think I will ask him what would happen should this scum have cancer.   <BR>I guess the citizens of Wichita will now also have to pay for medical expenses????????<!--/Text--></td></tr>
