<!--Post: 13171--><!--Time: 1114452007-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13171"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 25, 2005 - 11:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The colon cancer thing is a massive load of crap, no pun intended. <BR> <BR>What a bizarre conclusion for them to reach. I am <b>very</b> curious to see why they have reached this conclusion. <BR> <BR>I could be imagining things, but it&#39;s weird to me that weeks after I post a <a href="http://www.planethuff.com/darkside/archives/cat_true_crime_unsolved.html#000643">blog entry detailing my theory that the Zodiac Killer could very well be a John Doe who committed suicide in 2003</a> while terminally ill with <b>colon cancer</b> the <i>Enquirer</i> comes out with this story about Denny the Deadly Dog Catcher. I mention Rader in the blog entry, but the focus is all on Zodiac and my idea. <BR> <BR>Before you laugh at my pre-Copernican worldview, note that I get anywhere from 400-1000 hits a day on my weblog, and I&#39;ve recently gotten hits from IPs owned by the likes of CBS, NBC, numerous publishing companies, <i>&#40;hell, even got a couple from the Pulitzer organization, likely a mistake on their part&#41;</i> - including Beattie&#39;s publisher, Penguin Putnam, probably pissed at my drubbing them more than I did the author for the condition of &#34;Nightmare.&#34;  <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t get the kind of huge traffic a site of Tom&#39;s might get, but very good for a &#39;blog. Could someone have read my goofy theory and gotten their wires crossed and developed this dumbass theory about Rader? Or is it just a funky coincidence? <BR> <BR>My inquiring mind wants to know, yo. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13171-->
<!--Post: 13173--><!--Time: 1114455967-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13173"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 25, 2005 - 12:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, nothing would shock me at this point.  However, DTDC having colon cancer wouldn&#39;t shock me either. <BR>He is at the appropriate age and all...and as far as the Profile goes...either the loss of a spouse, an illness, etc... <BR>And then again, it probably WAS derived by your simple and innocent blog entry<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13173-->
<!--Post: 13174--><!--Time: 1114456071-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13174"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 25, 2005 - 12:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Being a first time &#34;board discussion&#34; member I have a really stupid question to ask &#40;well 2&#41; <BR>1.  What does lol mean <BR>2.  What does BTW mean? <BR>Thank you in advance for your time<!--/Text--></td></tr>
