<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13181"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 25, 2005 - 4:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Serial murderers will use an illness, psychological disorder, physical impairment or a religious experience in an attempt to contol and manipulate the judiciary. Rader is primarily concerned with receiving a lenient punishment. He would prefer serving life without the possibility of parole lying in a hammock than lying on a concrete floor. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
