<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13249"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nick<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nick<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->4-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 27, 2005 - 6:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->And don&#39;t forget the ever present...... <BR> <BR>ROFLMAO  &#40;rolling on floor laughing my a&#42;&#42; off&#41; <BR> <BR>The one I despise the most is &#34;k&#34; for ok. I mean WTF, it&#39;s a 2 letter word.  <BR> <BR>OMFG, I&#39;ve finally fallen prey to to these nerdy acronyms, lol. No need for a &#34;cheat book&#34;. There are numerous sites dedicated to internet acronyms. Here&#39;s a pretty good one... <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.acronymdictionary.co.uk" target=_top>http://www.acronymdictionary.co.uk</a>  <BR> <BR>BTW, it&#39;s nice to see a lot of the BTK sleuths taking an active interest in the zodiac case. We can only benefit from some fresh insight and perspective. All in all a very nice byproduct of Tom&#39;s efforts with this site.      <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13249-->
<!--Post: 13260--><!--Time: 1114701080-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13260"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 28, 2005 - 8:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I thought that LOL was lots of luck. You learn something new everyday. Colon cancer: maybe he hid some mementos &#39;up there&#39; and it is coming back to haunt him. One of his haunts might have been the bathroom. <BR> <BR>Going to trial: I do believe that despite the trauma to his family, Rader would feel vindicated by a trial and the world getting to know him. If he prepared massive documents for a $25 fine, imagine what he would have for his trial! And he will report every minutia. I don&#39;t think that he believes himself crazy either.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13260-->
<!--Post: 13265--><!--Time: 1114716898-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13265"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 28, 2005 - 12:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Nick, The Z case is very interesting to me. If I would have thought about it, I would have been there earlier since Rader was copying Z to a point. BTW I don&#39;t believe Rader is dying. But if he has cancer. Well I agree with the others, who cares. I don&#39;t feel sorry for him. This is another attempt to get attention. Trial? Well I have mixed feelings about that. Who would like to forget all the mistakes and make this go away?  A few people come to mind. So I guess we will have to see, If he gets to trial.          <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13265-->
<!--Post: 13266--><!--Time: 1114718136-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13266"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 28, 2005 - 12:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Quote&#62;&#62;&#62;Cow Town is Calgary, Alberta, Canada.&#60;&#60;&#60; <BR> <BR>Sorry for stealing Calgary&#39;s thunder. LOL <BR> <BR>I should have said Wichita&#39;s nickname is Cowtown. Although Doo-Dah is more dear to some people. LOL <BR>-Deb  <BR> <BR>Quote&#62;&#62;&#62;What&#39;s in a name? <BR> <BR>If you think recent slogans to boost tourism are lame, consider some past brainstorms that Wichita leaders used to lure newcomers: <BR> <BR>The Bride of Fortune, The Happy Valley, The Pride of the Prairies, The Darling of Destiny. <BR> <BR>But wait, it gets better: <BR> <BR>The Athens of the Midwest, The New Chicago, The Detroit of the Small Plane Age. <BR> <BR>And best of all: <BR> <BR>Peerless Princess of the Plains, The Magical Mascot of the Meridian, The Athletic Ajax of the Aboundful Arkansas and The Wonderfully Worthy Wombat. <BR> <BR>Air Capital of the World sounds pretty good about now.&#60;&#60;&#60; <BR> <BR>excerpt from this article: <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/entertainment/11296765.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/entertainment/112 96765.htm</a> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13266-->
<!--Post: 13274--><!--Time: 1114736141-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13274"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 28, 2005 - 5:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I like &#34;People of the Southwind&#34;. That was a great song by non-other than Kansas. &#40;Point of No Return&#41; God knows it blows like a SOB in Kansas.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13274-->
<!--Post: 13278--><!--Time: 1114740260-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13278"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 28, 2005 - 7:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How about a new slogan: <BR>Wichita, free of BTK since 2005.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13278-->
<!--Post: 13338--><!--Time: 1115102935-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13338"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 02, 2005 - 11:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Else: <BR> <BR>If someone becomes so ill that they either cannot assist in their defense or they no longer understand the nature of the legal proceedings, they cannot be tried until they recover.   <BR> <BR>If they never recover, they are never convicted. <BR> <BR>Phoenix<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13338-->
<!--Post: 13354--><!--Time: 1115133642-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13354"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 03, 2005 - 8:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->OMG - well, I guess it wouldn&#39;t be all that bad to know the sob is dying and suffering in jail...conviction or no conviction. <BR>But only if the public and the victims family could make the decision on whether or not he is to be provided treatment!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
